What the C actually contains, and how I handled it:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- **Only one external symbol.** [38;5;10mlib.h[0m declares [38;5;10mget_predict_func[0m, but [38;5;10mlib.c[0m never defines it — it defines [38;5;10mcall_predict[0m instead. There are no namespace-renaming macros anywhere, so the final linker symbol is plain [38;5;10mcall_predict[0m. I did not invent a [38;5;10mget_predict_func[0m, since the C [38;5;10m.so[0m doesn't have one either.[0m[0m
- **The 13 predictor functions plus [38;5;10mBTAC1C2_GetPredictFunc[0m are [38;5;10mstatic[0m**, so they are private in Rust. They still exist as real, non-inlined, address-taken functions because [38;5;10mcall_predict[0m compares function [3maddresses[23m, not results — the observable output depends on those addresses being distinct. [38;5;10m#[inline(never)][0m guards against the compiler collapsing them.[0m[0m
- **Two discrepancies in the C are preserved, not fixed:** [38;5;10mPfn10[0m shifts right by 3 where [38;5;10mcase 10:[0m of the big switch shifts by 4, and [38;5;10mPfn11[0m shifts by 1 where [38;5;10mcase 11:[0m shifts by 3. Comments mark both.[0m[0m
